      "file_type": "rationale",
      "norm_label": "adaptive contrast enhancement via local statistics",
      "rationale": "Each pixel is pushed away from its local mean by alpha*(1 - normalized local std), so homogeneous low-contrast regions are boosted more than already high-variance regions; chosen to avoid the over/under-enhancement of global histogram equalization and the noise amplification of AHE.",
